;; What was measured on 2026-09-09 while attempting the whole-component build,
;; and what was NOT. The `:blocked` disposition recorded for this tranche rests
;; on a gap table; most of that table does not reproduce.
{:as-of "2026-09-09"
 :amu-checkout-caveat
 "bin/amu was run from orgs/kotoba-lang/amu, which had 584 uncommitted files
  from a concurrent session. `check` and `compile` results below are therefore
  measured against a working tree, not against the pinned commit. A clean
  worktree at the pin cannot run bin/amu at all -- it has no node_modules --
  so this caveat could not be removed here."

 :constructs-the-gap-table-called-blocking
 ;; Each is one minimal probe under `amu check --jvm-free`, probes in
 ;; ../../q9-probes and reproducible.
 {:string-literal            :pass   ; (defn label [] :string "hello")
  :string-concat             :pass   ; the head is string-concat, not str
  :string=                   :pass
  :string-substring          :pass
  :count-over-list           :pass   ; [:list :i64]; [:vector ...] is not the type
  :vector-of-maps-constant   :pass   ; (def specs [{:entity "..."} {...}])
  :map-constant              :pass}

 :capability-imports
 ;; ADR-q9: a clock or an entropy source crosses as a DECLARED CAPABILITY
 ;; IMPORT and is not a reason to keep a component in Clojure. Both of this
 ;; component's mechanisms are reachable.
 {:clock/now    {:wire-id 7  :status :pass}
  :entropy/draw {:wire-id 23 :status :pass}
  :form "(ns … (:capabilities #{:clock/now :entropy/draw})) then (clock/now x)"
  :policy "{:allow #{[:cap/call 7] [:cap/call 23]}}"
  :note "amu refuses a capability declared but never called, and refuses a
         call the policy does not grant. Both refusals were observed."}

 :built
 {:check   {:command "amu check --jvm-free --policy policy.edn" :result :ok}
  :compile {:command "amu compile --target aarch64-macos --policy policy.edn"
            :result :ok :bytes 5577}}

 :not-done
 ;; Stated plainly because the skill's rule is that a build is not acceptance.
 {:artifact-not-executed
  "`amu extract-native --symbol main` answers `internal compiler error` -- on
   this component, on amu's own examples/todo-app.kotoba, and on a minimal
   `(defn main [] :i64 42)`. It is therefore NOT specific to this component.
   It is also NOT attributed: the amu checkout is dirty (above), and the clean
   worktree cannot run. So the artifact has not been executed and this
   component is NOT accepted."
  :component-is-partial
  "What compiles here is the data table, the derived route paths, the
   pagination decision and the two capability imports. The coercion layer
   (as-int/as-float/as-bool over untrusted strings), the store, validation,
   filters and the five handlers are NOT written. Calling this a
   whole-component build would be the decision-core framing the ADR forbids,
   one level up."}

 :consequence-for-the-tranche
 "The nine remaining wave-1 pilots are one template: 215 lines each, differing
  in 36 -- the entity table and the ns docstring. Their existing `.kotoba`
  files are decision-core slices whose own comments say `no strings, no maps,
  no folds` and `strings are outside the admitted subset`. That premise is
  false. Requalifying them is one judgement applied nine times, not nine
  investigations -- but the judgement needs a whole component that RUNS, and
  that is blocked on extract-native, not on the language."}
